": 0, "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "pdf", "content": "engenn9le02ob03re7pdf01.pdf"}]}]}], "template_override": 1, "id": 11, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " \nPractice using the third conditional!\n"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Take Away"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "\nInstructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment.\n"}]}]}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": []}, {"contents": [{"type": "video", "value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"time": "100", "image": "", "id": 1, "text": "If you have ever tried to grow plants, you know that plants need a warm environment. For this reason, plants are being grown in glass greenhouses. The glass traps the warm air inside so that the plants can grow.<br/>\nThis happens on the Earth as well. Gases found naturally in the atmosphere trap the heat of the sun, and warm up the Earth to a comfortable 59 degrees Fahrenheit. This has been called the \"greenhouse effect\", which makes it possible for humans, animals, and plants to live. If there were no gases in the atmosphere, the Earth would be a frozen snowball."}, {"time": "37500", "image": "", "id": 2, "text": "Many scientists say that human activities have caused greenhouse gases, such as carbon dioxide, to build up in the atmosphere. According to this theory, whenever we burn fossil fuels, such as gasoline, oil, coal, or natural gas, more greenhouse gases are being released into the atmosphere. As a result, the atmosphere is trapping more heat, and the earth is warming up. This theory is known as global warming."}, {"time": "66500", "image": "", "id": 3, "text": "Some scientists claim that global warming will take generations to affect the Earth. Others predict that if we do not reduce the release of greenhouse gases now, global temperatures will rise several degrees within the next 100 years. This change in temperature could mean major climate changes throughout the world.<br/>\nScientists claim that if we had acted earlier, humankind wouldn't have found themselves in this predicament. Once greenhouse gases have been released into the atmosphere, most of them remain there for decades and continue to trap heat."}], "video_src": "engenn9le02ob03re2vid01"}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "video", "id": 2, "_data": []}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}]}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "The Environment"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Global Warming"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe environmental change in social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. <br/> Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. <br/> Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Third Conditional"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are four types of conditional sentences in English:<ol><li>Zero Conditional - to talk about certainty and facts</li><li>First Conditional - to talk about real possibilities in the present or the future</li><li>Second Conditional - to talk about <span class=\"italic\">unreal</span> possibilities in the present or the future</li><li>Third Conditional - to talk about unreal <span class=\"italic\">past</span> situations</li></ol>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use third conditional to talk about unreal situations in the past. These are things that did not happen in the past. You often use the third conditional to talk about regrets."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart below to compare the structure of each kind of conditional:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Conditional Name</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Structure</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Example</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Zero \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span> + Simple Present, Simple Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If you <span class=\\\"strong\\\">heat</span> ice, it <span class=\\\"strong\\\">melts</span>.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"First\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span> + Simple Present, <span class=\\\"italic\\\">will</span> + Simple Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If we <span class=\\\"strong\\\">do not reduce</span> the release of greenhouse gases now, global temperatures <span class=\\\"strong\\\">will rise</span>.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Second\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span> + Simple Past, <span class=\\\"italic\\\">would</span> + Simple Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If there <span class=\\\"strong\\\">were</span> no gases in the atmosphere, the Earth <span class=\\\"strong\\\">would be</span> a frozen snowball.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Third\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span> + Past Perfect, <span class=\\\"italic\\\">would have</span> + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If we <span class=\\\"strong\\\">had acted</span> earlier, humankind <span class=\\\"strong\\\">wouldn't have found themselves</span> in this predicament.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If there were no gases in the atmosphere, the Earth would be a frozen snowball."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If we do not reduce the release of greenhouse gases now, global temperatures will rise several degrees within the next 100 years."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Scientists claim that if we had acted earlier, humankind wouldn't have found themselves in this predicament."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Passive: The Present Continuous and Present Perfect Tenses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>You use the Present Continuous to talk about an action that is happening at the time of speaking. The action or event is in progress. <br/><span class=\"italic\">As a result, the atmosphere <span class=\"strong\">is trapping</span> more heat, and the earth <span class=\"strong\">is warming up</span>.</span></p><p>You use the Present Perfect to talk about a finished action or event with present consequences. There is a connection between what happened in the past and the present.<br/><span class=\"italic\">Many scientists say that human activities <span class=\"strong\">have caused</span> greenhouse gases to build up in the atmosphere. </span></p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You often choose the passive form when you want to talk about an action but are not so interested in saying who or what does/did it. Passives without <span class=\"italic\">agents</span> (the doers) are common in academic and scientific writing. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart below for the structure of the passive voice."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Name\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">am</span>/<span class=\\\"italic\\\">are</span>/<span class=\\\"italic\\\">is</span> +  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">being </span>+ past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Whenever we burn fossil fuels, more greenhouse gases <span class=\\\"strong\\\">are being released</span> into the atmosphere. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">have</span>/<span class=\\\"italic\\\">has</span> + <span class=\\\"italic\\\">been </span>+ past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Once greenhouse gases <span class=\\\"strong\\\">have been released</span> into the atmosphere, most of them remain there for decades and continue to trap heat.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "This has been called the \"greenhouse effect\", which makes it possible for humans, animals, and plants to live. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Once greenhouse gases have been released into the atmosphere, most of them remain there for decades and continue to trap heat."}, {"type": "example", "content": "According to this theory, whenever we burn fossil fuels, such as gasoline, oil, coal, or natural gas, more greenhouse gases are being released into the atmosphere. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "For this reason, plants are being grown in glass greenhouses. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "As a result, the atmosphere is trapping more heat, and the earth is warming up. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to grow"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to increase in amount, size, number, or strength"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Plants need a warm environment to grow in."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le02ob03aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about the greenhouse effect."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "greenhouse "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a small glass building used to grow plants all year round"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Plants are being grown in glass greenhouses."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le02ob03aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to trap"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to prevent something from escaping from somewhere"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The glass traps the warm air inside so that the plants can grow."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le02ob03aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "snowball "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a ball formed by packing snow tightly together"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If there were no gases in the atmosphere, the Earth would be a frozen snowball.   "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le02ob03aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to build up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to construct"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Human activities have caused carbon dioxide, to build up in the atmosphere."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le02ob03aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fossil fuel"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a combustible organic material, such as oil, coal, or natural gas."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Whenever we burn fossil fuels, such as gasoline, oil, coal, or natural gas, more greenhouse gases are being released."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le02ob03aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "coal "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a hard black mineral burned to produce heat"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Coal is a fossil fuel that causes global warming."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le02ob03aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "release "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "allowing to flow out of a usual container"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If we do not reduce the release of greenhouse gases now, global temperatures will rise several degrees within the next 100 years."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le02ob03aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "predicament "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a difficult or unpleasant situation where you have to make a difficult choice"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If we had acted earlier, humankind wouldn't have found themselves in this predicament."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le02ob03aud09"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "On 8 small pieces of paper, write down 4 nouns related to the environment and four verbs related to the environment."}, {"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, take turns choosing one noun and one verb and making third conditional sentences with them.  <br/> For example: garbage, dispose = If I had disposed of my garbage, my house would not have been dirty."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you have finished your words, think of new sentences and discuss the conditions that you created."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I talk about the environment."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about unreal conditions in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I discuss the conditions with a partner."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le02ob03re1img01.jpg"}]}